# Netlify serves this file's rules with every response. It is here to state the
# caching policy explicitly instead of relying on a platform default: an
# intermediate proxy that sees no directive is free to invent one, and a stale
# app.js behind a fresh index.html is exactly how a deploy comes out looking
# half-updated.
#
# Nothing is cached hard on purpose. Deliberately NOT "immutable": the ?v=
# strings in index.html are maintained by hand, so a forgotten bump must fail
# safe (revalidate, get the new file) rather than pin everyone to a stale copy.

/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate

# The one file with no version string of its own, so it must never be held.
/
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
